AB  - e purpose of this study is to contribute to improving the environment of Eco Delta City by predicting fine dust concentrations using artificial intelligence in Eco Delta City, Busan collected from public observatories. To this end, we collected air quality and weather data from the national measurement network Air Korea and the Meteorological Data Open Portal for the past two years from 2021 to 2022, and collected PM2.5, PM10, SO2, NO2, CO, O3, and temperature in Eco Delta City, the correlation between humidity, wind direction, wind speed, and precipitation variables was identified. In addition, hourly PM2.5 concentrations in Eco Delta City were predicted using Random Forest, XGBoost and DNN.s a result of the prediction, the RMSE values were 3.676, 1.884, and 3.663, respectively, showing very high performance in all individual models compared to the Air Korea prediction model of 5.983. In particular, the XGBoost model showed results that were about 68.5% higher than the Air Korea model
